  "title": { "en": "Numbers, Time & Money", "so": "Tirooyinka, Waqtiga iyo Lacagta" },
  "swTitle": "Namba, Saa na Pesa",
  "description": {
    "en": "Count, tell Swahili time, ask prices, bargain at the market and pay the Kenyan way with M-Pesa.",
    "so": "Tiri, sheeg waqtiga Sawaaxiliga, weydii qiimaha, ku gorgortan suuqa oo ku bixi M-Pesa sida Kenya."
  },
  "guide": [
    {
      "title": { "en": "Some numbers come from Arabic", "so": "Tirooyinka qaar waxay ka yimaadeen Carabi" },
      "body": {
        "en": "Sita (6), saba (7) and tisa (9) come from Arabic sitta, sab'a and tis'a. So do ishirini (20), thelathini (30), arobaini (40), hamsini (50), mia (100) and elfu (1,000). Somali uses its own words (lix, toddoba, sagaal), but if you know Arabic numbers these will feel familiar.",
        "so": "Sita (6), saba (7) iyo tisa (9) waxay ka yimaadeen Carabiga sitta, sabca iyo tisca. Sidoo kale ishirini (20), thelathini (30), arobaini (40), hamsini (50), mia (100) iyo elfu (1,000). Soomaaligu wuxuu leeyahay erayo u gaar ah (lix, toddoba, sagaal), laakiin haddii aad taqaanno tirooyinka Carabiga, kuwani way kuu yaqaannaan."
      },
      "examples": [
        { "sw": "sita, saba, tisa", "en": "six, seven, nine", "so": "lix, toddoba, sagaal", "v": "standard" },
        { "sw": "mia moja, elfu moja", "en": "one hundred, one thousand", "so": "boqol, kun", "v": "standard" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": { "en": "Swahili time starts at 6 a.m.", "so": "Waqtiga Sawaaxiligu wuxuu ka bilaabmaa 6-da subaxnimo" },
      "body": {
        "en": "In Swahili time the day starts at sunrise. Saa moja (hour one) is 7 o'clock, saa mbili is 8, saa sita is 12. The easy rule: subtract 6 from the English hour. Kenyans use Swahili time when they speak Swahili, but often switch to English time in English.",
        "so": "Waqtiga Sawaaxiliga maalintu waxay ka bilaabataa qorrax soo baxa. Saa moja (saacadda koowaad) waa 7-da, saa mbili waa 8-da, saa sita waa 12-ka. Xeerka fudud: 6 ka jar saacadda Ingiriisiga. Kenyaanku waxay isticmaalaan waqtiga Sawaaxiliga markay Sawaaxili ku hadlayaan, laakiin badanaa waqtiga Ingiriisiga ayay u wareegaan markay Ingiriis ku hadlayaan."
      },
      "examples": [
        { "sw": "saa moja asubuhi", "en": "7 a.m.", "so": "7-da subaxnimo", "v": "standard" },
        { "sw": "saa nne na nusu", "en": "10:30", "so": "10:30", "v": "standard" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": { "en": "Kenyan money talk", "so": "Hadalka lacagta Kenya" },
      "body": {
        "en": "Prices are in Kenyan shillings (KSh). Kenyans often say bob for shillings: mia bob is 100 shillings. Most people pay with M-Pesa on the phone: Lipa na M-Pesa. In Tanzania the same sign says Lipa kwa M-Pesa.",
        "so": "Qiimaha waxaa lagu qoraa shilinka Kenya (KSh). Kenyaanku badanaa shilinka waxay u yaqaannaan bob: mia bob waa 100 shilin. Dadka badankiisu waxay ku bixiyaan M-Pesa taleefanka: Lipa na M-Pesa. Tanzania calaamadda la midka ah waxay leedahay Lipa kwa M-Pesa."
      },
      "examples": [
        { "sw": "Lipa na M-Pesa", "en": "Pay with M-Pesa", "so": "Ku bixi M-Pesa", "v": "everyday" },
        { "sw": "Ni mia bob.", "en": "It's 100 shillings.", "so": "Waa 100 shilin.", "v": "everyday" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": { "en": "How to bargain", "so": "Sida loo gorgortamo" },
      "body": {
        "en": "Greet first, then ask Ni pesa ngapi? If it is too much, say Ni ghali! and Punguza kidogo with a smile. Prices at markets and with mama mboga (vegetable sellers) are often open to a little bargaining. Supermarket prices are fixed.",
        "so": "Marka hore salaan, kadib weydii Ni pesa ngapi? Haddii ay aad u badan tahay, dheh Ni ghali! iyo Punguza kidogo adigoo dhoola caddaynaya. Qiimaha suuqyada iyo mama mboga (iibiyeyaasha khudaarta) badanaa wax yar ayaa laga gorgortami karaa. Qiimaha suubarmaarkeetka waa go'an yahay."
      }
    }
  ],
